{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c435","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b225-c4f5-7551-94b6-c0c601dc074b"},"sequence":117,"recorded_at":1780531400000229,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac"},"call_id":"call_01a0b225f88b74189398e0269a00732b","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/clonebundle/doc.go`.\n1|package clonebundle\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts:\n4|// Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (with\n5|// Capture Items, Capture Source Basis, and Capture Boundary), Canonical\n6|// Session 1.0.0, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (with Source Evidence and raw\n7|// references), the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, raw\n8|// evidence descriptor agreement over Section 10.2 Blob Descriptors,\n9|// reverse-DNS extension keys, and immutable source generations.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md; the\n13|// pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n14|//\n15|// Every Decode entry validates a closed shape: exact members, bounded\n16|// scalars, closed vocabularies, sorted-unique order, and self-digest\n17|// agreement. Every Build entry constructs the same bytes\n18|// deterministically: identical inputs produce byte-identical outputs,\n19|// and every Build output decodes clean. Refusals name the offending\n20|// member and never admit a partial object.\n21|//\n22|// Reuse, not fork: Environment Tuples decode through\n23|// sessadapter.DecodeTuple, Blob Descriptors verify through\n24|// canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity plus a local claim comparison\n25|// (never the attesting entry, per the provhost no-attestation bound),\n26|// extension keys admit through\n27|// environ.CheckExtensions, and blob bytes install through\n28|// localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob. The canonicaljson closed-shape\n29|// registry keeps its rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape rows for\n30|// these schemas (that table's census pins every row, so replacing\n31|// them would fork ownership); this package is the validating owner\n32|// and says so here and in TRACEABILITY.md.\n33|//\n34|// Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind Canonical Event\n35|// payload fact registries beyond the Section 13.14.1 envelope rules\n36|// enforced here (which facts a kind may carry; the Section 1.6 value\n37|// model on every payload member is enforced here);\n38|// maximal_safe projection gating past the raw_complete=false\n39|// derivation; target-branch (G2) admission beyond\n40|// RefuseUnstableForTarget; capture-plan/capture/normalize adapter\n41|// operation wiring (Section 7.8 bodies stay owned by sessadapter).\n42|// This package performs no durable write itself: blob installation\n43|// delegates to the landed localstore no-replace discipline, and the\n44|// crash/idempotency evidence for that path is cited in\n45|// TRACEABILITY.md.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c437","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b225-c4f5-7551-94b6-c0c601dc074b"},"sequence":118,"recorded_at":1780531400000231,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac"},"call_id":"call_01a0b225fa587494901d3389f59621a0","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/clonebundle/capturebuild.go`.\n1|package clonebundle\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"sort\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file validates and constructs Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0:\n12|// the closed envelope over source basis, capture boundary, sorted\n13|// Capture Items, exact excluded classes, and the core-derived\n14|// raw_complete flag.\n15|\n16|const (\n17|\tcaptureManifestSchema  = \"urn:ax:schema:clone-capture-manifest\"\n18|\tcaptureManifestVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n19|\tcaptureManifestSelf    = \"capture_manifest_id\"\n20|)\n21|\n22|var captureManifestMembers = map[string]bool{\n23|\t\"schema\": true, \"schema_version\": true, \"capture_manifest_id\": true,\n24|\t\"operation_id\": true, \"bundle_id\": true, \"source_basis\": true,\n25|\t\"source_environment\": true, \"source_identity\": true,\n26|\t\"capture_plan_digest\": true, \"capture_boundary\": true,\n27|\t\"source_raw_object_manifest_id\": true, \"items\": true,\n28|\t\"excluded_classes\": true, \"raw_complete\": true,\n29|\t\"created_by_host_id\": true, \"created_at\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n30|}\n31|\n32|var captureManifestRequired = []string{\n33|\t\"schema\", \"schema_version\", \"capture_manifest_id\",\n34|\t\"operation_id\", \"bundle_id\", \"source_basis\",\n35|\t\"source_environment\", \"source_identity\",\n36|\t\"capture_plan_digest\", \"capture_boundary\",\n37|\t\"source_raw_object_manifest_id\", \"items\",\n38|\t\"excluded_classes\", \"raw_complete\",\n39|\t\"created_by_host_id\", \"created_at\", \"extensions\",\n40|}\n41|\n42|// CaptureManifest is one validated Clone Capture Manifest.\n43|type CaptureManifest struct {\n44|\tManifestID              scalar.Digest\n45|\tOperationID             scalar.UUIDv7\n46|\tBundleID                scalar.UUIDv7\n47|\tSourceBasis             SourceBasis\n48|\tSourceEnvironment       sessadapter.Tuple\n49|\tSourceIdentity          NativeIdentity\n50|\tCapturePlanDigest       scalar.Digest\n51|\tCaptureBoundary         CaptureBoundary\n52|\tSourceRawObjectManifest scalar.Digest\n53|\tItems                   []CaptureItem\n54|\tExcludedClasses         []string\n55|\tRawComplete             bool\n56|\tCreatedByHostID         scalar.UUIDv7\n57|\tCreatedAt               scalar.Timestamp\n58|}\n59|\n60|// CaptureManifestInput is the caller-supplied capture manifest\n61|// candidate for Build. PlanKeys are the exact capture-plan\n62|// candidate keys and RawKeys are the exact raw-manifest entry keys;\n63|// raw_complete is core-derived from them and is not an input — a\n64|// caller cannot assert completeness, only the reconciliation can.\n65|type CaptureManifestInput struct {\n66|\tOperationID         string\n67|\tBundleID            string\n68|\tSourceBasis         SourceBasisInput\n69|\tSourceEnvironment   []byte\n70|\tSourceIdentity      NativeIdentity\n71|\tIdentityExtensions  map[string]any\n72|\tCapturePlanDigest   string\n73|\tBoundary            BoundaryInput\n74|\tSourceRawManifestID string\n75|\tItems               []CaptureItemInput\n76|\tPlanKeys            []string\n77|\tRawKeys             []string\n78|\tCreatedByHostID     string\n79|\tCreatedAt           string\n80|\tExtensions          map[string]any\n81|}\n82|\n83|// BuildCaptureManifest constructs one closed Clone Capture Manifest\n84|// as canonical bytes. Identical inputs produce byte-identical\n85|// outputs. raw_complete is derived, never accepted: it is true only\n86|// after complete plan/object reconciliation with no unknown class.\n87|func BuildCaptureManifest(input CaptureManifestInput) ([]byte, error) {\n88|\t_, object, err := buildCaptureManifest(input)\n89|\tif err != nil {\n90|\t\treturn nil, err\n91|\t}\n92|\tomitted, err := canonicalizeObject(object)\n93|\tif err != nil {\n94|\t\treturn nil, err\n95|\t}\n96|\tmanifestID := scalar.SHA256Digest(omitted)\n97|\tobject[captureManifestSelf] = manifestID.String()\n98|\treturn canonicalizeObject(object)\n99|}\n100|\n101|func buildCaptureManifest(input CaptureManifestInput) (CaptureManifest, map[string]any, error) {\n102|\toperation, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(input.OperationID)\n103|\tif err != nil {\n104|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest operation_id is not a UUIDv7: %v\", err)\n105|\t}\n106|\tbundle, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(input.BundleID)\n107|\tif err != nil {\n108|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest bundle_id is not a UUIDv7: %v\", err)\n109|\t}\n110|\tbasis, basisObject, err := buildSourceBasis(input.SourceBasis)\n111|\tif err != nil {\n112|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n113|\t}\n114|\ttuple, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(json.RawMessage(input.SourceEnvironment))\n115|\tif err != nil {\n116|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest source_environment is not an Environment Tuple: %v\", err)\n117|\t}\n118|\tidentityBytes, err := EncodeNativeIdentity(input.SourceIdentity, input.IdentityExtensions)\n119|\tif err != nil {\n120|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n121|\t}\n122|\tif _, err := DecodeNativeIdentity(json.RawMessage(identityBytes)); err != nil {\n123|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest source_identity is not a NativeIdentity: %v\", err)\n124|\t}\n125|\tplanDigest, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.CapturePlanDigest)\n126|\tif err != nil {\n127|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest capture_plan_digest is not a digest: %v\", err)\n128|\t}\n129|\tboundary, boundaryObject, err := buildBoundary(input.Boundary)\n130|\tif err != nil {\n131|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n132|\t}\n133|\trawManifestID, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.SourceRawManifestID)\n134|\tif err != nil {\n135|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest source_raw_object_manifest_id is not a digest: %v\", err)\n136|\t}\n137|\tif len(input.Items) > 65536 {\n138|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest carries %d items, maximum is 65536\", len(input.Items))\n139|\t}\n140|\titems := make([]CaptureItem, 0, len(input.Items))\n141|\tprevious := \"\"\n142|\tfor index, candidate := range input.Items {\n143|\t\titem, err := buildCaptureItem(candidate, index)\n144|\t\tif err != nil {\n145|\t\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n146|\t\t}\n147|\t\tif index > 0 && item.NativeItemKey <= previous {\n148|\t\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest items are not sorted bytewise by native item key\")\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t\tprevious = item.NativeItemKey\n151|\t\titems = append(items, item)\n152|\t}\n153|\tif err := checkPlanItemMatch(items, input.PlanKeys); err != nil {\n154|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n155|\t}\n156|\texcluded := excludedRowClasses(items)\n157|\trawComplete := deriveRawComplete(items, input.PlanKeys, input.RawKeys)\n158|\thostID, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(input.CreatedByHostID)\n159|\tif err != nil {\n160|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest created_by_host_id is not a UUIDv7: %v\", err)\n161|\t}\n162|\tcreatedAt, err := scalar.ParseTimestamp(input.CreatedAt)\n163|\tif err != nil {\n164|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest created_at is not a timestamp: %v\", err)\n165|\t}\n166|\tif _, err := encodeExtensions(input.Extensions); err != nil {\n167|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, err\n168|\t}\n169|\tvar identityValue any\n170|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(identityBytes, &identityValue); err != nil {\n171|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, nil, invalid(\"capture manifest source_identity is not JSON: %v\", err)\n172|\t}\n173|\tobjects := make([]any, 0, len(items))\n174|\tfor _, item := range items {\n175|\t\tobjects = append(objects, captureItemObject(item))\n176|\t}\n177|\texcludedValue := make([]any, 0, len(excluded))\n178|\tfor _, class := range excluded {\n179|\t\texcludedValue = append(excludedValue, class)\n180|\t}\n181|\tmanifest := CaptureManifest{\n182|\t\tOperationID:             operation,\n183|\t\tBundleID:                bundle,\n184|\t\tSourceBasis:             basis,\n185|\t\tSourceEnvironment:       tuple,\n186|\t\tSourceIdentity:          input.SourceIdentity,\n187|\t\tCapturePlanDigest:       planDigest,\n188|\t\tCaptureBoundary:         boundary,\n189|\t\tSourceRawObjectManifest: rawManifestID,\n190|\t\tItems:                   items,\n191|\t\tExcludedClasses:         excluded,\n192|\t\tRawComplete:             rawComplete,\n193|\t\tCreatedByHostID:         hostID,\n194|\t\tCreatedAt:               createdAt,\n195|\t}\n196|\tobject := map[string]any{\n197|\t\t\"schema\":                        captureManifestSchema,\n198|\t\t\"schema_version\":                captureManifestVersion,\n199|\t\t\"operation_id\":                  operation.String(),\n200|\t\t\"bundle_id\":                     bundle.String(),\n201|\t\t\"source_basis\":                  basisObject,\n202|\t\t\"source_environment\":            tupleObject(tuple),\n203|\t\t\"source_identity\":               identityValue,\n204|\t\t\"capture_plan_digest\":           planDigest.String(),\n205|\t\t\"capture_boundary\":              boundaryObject,\n206|\t\t\"source_raw_object_manifest_id\": rawManifestID.String(),\n207|\t\t\"items\":                         objects,\n208|\t\t\"excluded_classes\":              excludedValue,\n209|\t\t\"raw_complete\":                  rawComplete,\n210|\t\t\"created_by_host_id\":            hostID.String(),\n211|\t\t\"created_at\":                    createdAt.String(),\n212|\t\t\"extensions\":                    extensionValue(input.Extensions),\n213|\t}\n214|\treturn manifest, object, nil\n215|}\n216|\n217|// DecodeCaptureManifest validates one closed Clone Capture Manifest:\n218|// exact members, schema/version, self-digest agreement, sorted\n219|// items, exact excluded classes, and the unknown-makes-incomplete\n220|// rule. Full plan/object reconciliation needs the plan and raw key\n221|// sets; VerifyCaptureReconciliation performs it.\n222|func DecodeCaptureManifest(data []byte) (CaptureManifest, error) {\n223|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(data)\n224|\tif fault != nil {\n225|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest %s (%s)\", fault.detail, memberField(fault.member))\n226|\t}\n227|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, captureManifestMembers); unknown {\n228|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest carries unknown member %q\", name)\n229|\t}\n230|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, captureManifestRequired); missing {\n231|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest misses a required member %q\", name)\n232|\t}\n233|\tschema, ok := rawString(members[\"schema\"])\n234|\tif !ok || schema != captureManifestSchema {\n235|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest schema is not the clone capture manifest\")\n236|\t}\n237|\tversion, ok := rawString(members[\"schema_version\"])\n238|\tif !ok || version != captureManifestVersion {\n239|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest version is not 1.0.0\")\n240|\t}\n241|\tmanifestID, ok := checkDigest(members[captureManifestSelf])\n242|\tif !ok {\n243|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest capture_manifest_id is not a digest\")\n244|\t}\n245|\toperation, ok := checkUUIDv7(members[\"operation_id\"])\n246|\tif !ok {\n247|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest operation_id is not a UUIDv7\")\n248|\t}\n249|\tbundle, ok := checkUUIDv7(members[\"bundle_id\"])\n250|\tif !ok {\n251|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest bundle_id is not a UUIDv7\")\n252|\t}\n253|\tbasis, err := DecodeSourceBasis(members[\"source_basis\"])\n254|\tif err != nil {\n255|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, err\n256|\t}\n257|\ttuple, err := sessadapter.DecodeTuple(members[\"source_environment\"])\n258|\tif err != nil {\n259|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest source_environment is not an Environment Tuple: %v\", err)\n260|\t}\n261|\tidentity, err := DecodeNativeIdentity(members[\"source_identity\"])\n262|\tif err != nil {\n263|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, err\n264|\t}\n265|\tplanDigest, ok := checkDigest(members[\"capture_plan_digest\"])\n266|\tif !ok {\n267|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest capture_plan_digest is not a digest\")\n268|\t}\n269|\tboundary, err := DecodeCaptureBoundary(members[\"capture_boundary\"])\n270|\tif err != nil {\n271|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, err\n272|\t}\n273|\trawManifestID, ok := checkDigest(members[\"source_raw_object_manifest_id\"])\n274|\tif !ok {\n275|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest source_raw_object_manifest_id is not a digest\")\n276|\t}\n277|\titems, err := decodeCaptureItems(members[\"items\"])\n278|\tif err != nil {\n279|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, err\n280|\t}\n281|\texcluded, ok := checkSortedUniqueStrings(members[\"excluded_classes\"], 1, 128, 0, 9)\n282|\tif !ok {\n283|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest excluded_classes are not sorted unique string[1..128][0..9]\")\n284|\t}\n285|\tfor _, class := range excluded {\n286|\t\tif !ValidCaptureClass(class) {\n287|\t\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest excluded_classes carry unknown class %q\", class)\n288|\t\t}\n289|\t}\n290|\tif !excludedClassesExact(items, excluded) {\n291|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest excluded_classes are not exactly the excluded-row classes\")\n292|\t}\n293|\trawComplete, ok := rawBool(members[\"raw_complete\"])\n294|\tif !ok {\n295|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest raw_complete is not a boolean\")\n296|\t}\n297|\tif rawComplete && hasUnknownClass(items) {\n298|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest raw_complete is true with an unknown-class item\")\n299|\t}\n300|\thostID, ok := checkUUIDv7(members[\"created_by_host_id\"])\n301|\tif !ok {\n302|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest created_by_host_id is not a UUIDv7\")\n303|\t}\n304|\tcreatedAt, ok := checkTimestamp(members[\"created_at\"])\n305|\tif !ok {\n306|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest created_at is not a timestamp\")\n307|\t}\n308|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n309|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, invalid(\"capture manifest extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n310|\t}\n311|\tif err := verifySelfDigest(members, captureManifestSelf, manifestID); err != nil {\n312|\t\treturn CaptureManifest{}, err\n313|\t}\n314|\treturn CaptureManifest{\n315|\t\tManifestID:              manifestID,\n316|\t\tOperationID:             operation,\n317|\t\tBundleID:                bundle,\n318|\t\tSourceBasis:             basis,\n319|\t\tSourceEnvironment:       tuple,\n320|\t\tSourceIdentity:          identity,\n321|\t\tCapturePlanDigest:       planDigest,\n322|\t\tCaptureBoundary:         boundary,\n323|\t\tSourceRawObjectManifest: rawManifestID,\n324|\t\tItems:                   items,\n325|\t\tExcludedClasses:         excluded,\n326|\t\tRawComplete:             rawComplete,\n327|\t\tCreatedByHostID:         hostID,\n328|\t\tCreatedAt:               createdAt,\n329|\t}, nil\n330|}\n331|\n332|func decodeCaptureItems(raw json.RawMessage) ([]CaptureItem, error) {\n333|\telements, ok := decodeArray(raw)\n334|\tif !ok {\n335|\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"capture manifest items are not an array\")\n336|\t}\n337|\tif len(elements) > 65536 {\n338|\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"capture manifest carries %d items, maximum is 65536\", len(elements))\n339|\t}\n340|\titems := make([]CaptureItem, 0, len(elements))\n341|\tprevious := \"\"\n342|\tfor index, element := range elements {\n343|\t\titem, err := decodeCaptureItem(element, index)\n344|\t\tif err != nil {\n345|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n346|\t\t}\n347|\t\tif index > 0 && item.NativeItemKey <= previous {\n348|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"capture manifest items are not sorted bytewise by native item key\")\n349|\t\t}\n350|\t\tprevious = item.NativeItemKey\n351|\t\titems = append(items, item)\n352|\t}\n353|\treturn items, nil\n354|}\n355|\n356|// checkPlanItemMatch enforces the one-per-plan-candidate rule at\n357|// construction: the sealed items must be exactly one per capture-plan\n358|// candidate, no missing and no extra. An incomplete raw closure still\n359|// seals (with raw_complete false), but an items/plan mismatch is a\n360|// malformed manifest, never an archive object. Duplicate plan keys\n361|// are refused outright: a repeated key would defeat the count and\n362|// hide an item that is not a plan candidate.\n363|func checkPlanItemMatch(items []CaptureItem, planKeys []string) error {\n364|\tif len(items) != len(planKeys) {\n365|\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest carries %d items for %d plan candidates, want one per plan candidate\", len(items), len(planKeys))\n366|\t}\n367|\tseenPlan := map[string]bool{}\n368|\tfor _, key := range planKeys {\n369|\t\tif seenPlan[key] {\n370|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest plan keys carry duplicate %q\", key)\n371|\t\t}\n372|\t\tseenPlan[key] = true\n373|\t}\n374|\titemSet := map[string]bool{}\n375|\tfor _, item := range items {\n376|\t\titemSet[item.NativeItemKey] = true\n377|\t}\n378|\tfor _, key := range planKeys {\n379|\t\tif !itemSet[key] {\n380|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest plan candidate %q has no item\", key)\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t}\n383|\treturn nil\n384|}\n385|\n386|// excludedRowClasses derives the exact excluded-row class set:\n387|// sorted unique classes of excluded rows.\n388|func excludedRowClasses(items []CaptureItem) []string {\n389|\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n390|\tfor _, item := range items {\n391|\t\tif !item.Included() {\n392|\t\t\tseen[item.Class] = true\n393|\t\t}\n394|\t}\n395|\tclasses := make([]string, 0, len(seen))\n396|\tfor class := range seen {\n397|\t\tclasses = append(classes, class)\n398|\t}\n399|\tsort.Strings(classes)\n400|\treturn classes\n401|}\n402|\n403|func excludedClassesExact(items []CaptureItem, excluded []string) bool {\n404|\tderived := excludedRowClasses(items)\n405|\tif len(derived) != len(excluded) {\n406|\t\treturn false\n407|\t}\n408|\tfor index := range derived {\n409|\t\tif derived[index] != excluded[index] {\n410|\t\t\treturn false\n411|\t\t}\n412|\t}\n413|\treturn true\n414|}\n415|\n416|func hasUnknownClass(items []CaptureItem) bool {\n417|\tfor _, item := range items {\n418|\t\tif item.Class == \"unknown\" {\n419|\t\t\treturn true\n420|\t\t}\n421|\t}\n422|\treturn false\n423|}\n424|\n425|// deriveRawComplete is the core raw_complete derivation: true only\n426|// when no item has unknown class, every plan candidate reconciles\n427|// to exactly one item, and the included items are exactly the raw\n428|// manifest keys (all and only included objects).\n429|func deriveRawComplete(items []CaptureItem, planKeys, rawKeys []string) bool {\n430|\tif hasUnknownClass(items) {\n431|\t\treturn false\n432|\t}\n433|\tif len(items) != len(planKeys) {\n434|\t\treturn false\n435|\t}\n436|\tplanSet := map[string]bool{}\n437|\tfor _, key := range planKeys {\n438|\t\tplanSet[key] = true\n439|\t}\n440|\tif len(planSet) != len(planKeys) {\n441|\t\treturn false\n442|\t}\n443|\tincluded := map[string]bool{}\n444|\tfor _, item := range items {\n445|\t\tif !planSet[item.NativeItemKey] {\n446|\t\t\treturn false\n447|\t\t}\n448|\t\tif item.Included() {\n449|\t\t\tincluded[item.NativeItemKey] = true\n450|\t\t}\n451|\t}\n452|\tif len(included) != len(rawKeys) {\n453|\t\treturn false\n454|\t}\n455|\tseenRaw := map[string]bool{}\n456|\tfor _, key := range rawKeys {\n457|\t\tif !included[key] {\n458|\t\t\treturn false\n459|\t\t}\n460|\t\tif seenRaw[key] {\n461|\t\t\treturn false\n462|\t\t}\n463|\t\tseenRaw[key] = true\n464|\t}\n465|\treturn true\n466|}\n467|\n468|// VerifyCaptureReconciliation re-checks complete plan/object\n469|// reconciliation for a decoded manifest: one item per plan\n470|// candidate, the raw closure over exactly the included items, and a\n471|// raw_complete flag that matches the derivation. Unknown classes\n472|// always reconcile to false. Duplicate raw keys are refused\n473|// outright: a duplicate would defeat the \"all\" half of the all-and-only\n474|// closure, hiding a missing included object behind a repeated key.\n475|func VerifyCaptureReconciliation(manifest CaptureManifest, planKeys, rawKeys []string) error {\n476|\tseenRaw := map[string]bool{}\n477|\tfor _, key := range rawKeys {\n478|\t\tif seenRaw[key] {\n479|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest raw keys carry duplicate %q\", key)\n480|\t\t}\n481|\t\tseenRaw[key] = true\n482|\t}\n483|\tderived := deriveRawComplete(manifest.Items, planKeys, rawKeys)\n484|\tif manifest.RawComplete != derived {\n485|\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest raw_complete is %v, reconciliation derives %v\", manifest.RawComplete, derived)\n486|\t}\n487|\tif !derived {\n488|\t\treturn invalid(\"capture manifest plan/object reconciliation is incomplete\")\n489|\t}\n490|\treturn nil\n491|}\n492|\n493|// RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete blocks the maximal_safe fidelity\n494|// profile: unknown classes block it, and it requires a reconciled\n495|// complete manifest. Projection planning calls this gate.\n496|func RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete(manifest CaptureManifest) error {\n497|\tif hasUnknownClass(manifest.Items) {\n498|\t\treturn invalid(\"maximal_safe is blocked by an unknown-class item\")\n499|\t}\n500|\tif !manifest.RawComplete {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c439","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b225-c4f5-7551-94b6-c0c601dc074b"},"sequence":119,"recorded_at":1780531400000233,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac"},"call_id":"call_01a0b225fc23761496d0cfd93ed44c18","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/clonebundle/boundary.go`.\n1|package clonebundle\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// This file validates the Capture Source Basis and Capture Boundary\n10|// closed unions of Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0, including the\n11|// StableSnapshotProof. The stable form carries proof; the unstable\n12|// form is core-created archive-only output that can never enter a\n13|// target branch.\n14|\n15|// SourceBasis is one validated Capture Source Basis.\n16|type SourceBasis struct {\n17|\tKind                     string\n18|\tSourceSessionID          *scalar.UUIDv7\n19|\tSourceSessionRecordID    *scalar.Digest\n20|\tSourceCheckpointID       *scalar.Digest\n21|\tSourceProviderIdentityID *scalar.Digest\n22|\tExternalSourceRef        *string\n23|}\n24|\n25|var sourceBasisAXMembers = map[string]bool{\n26|\t\"kind\": true, \"source_session_id\": true, \"source_session_record_id\": true,\n27|\t\"source_checkpoint_id\": true, \"source_provider_identity_record_id\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n28|}\n29|\n30|var sourceBasisAXRequired = []string{\n31|\t\"kind\", \"source_session_id\", \"source_session_record_id\",\n32|\t\"source_checkpoint_id\", \"source_provider_identity_record_id\", \"extensions\",\n33|}\n34|\n35|var sourceBasisExternalMembers = map[string]bool{\n36|\t\"kind\": true, \"external_source_ref\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n37|}\n38|\n39|var sourceBasisExternalRequired = []string{\n40|\t\"kind\", \"external_source_ref\", \"extensions\",\n41|}\n42|\n43|// DecodeSourceBasis validates one closed Capture Source Basis.\n44|func DecodeSourceBasis(raw json.RawMessage) (SourceBasis, error) {\n45|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n46|\tif fault != nil {\n47|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis %s (%s)\", fault.detail, memberField(fault.member))\n48|\t}\n49|\tkindValue, present := members[\"kind\"]\n50|\tif !present {\n51|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis misses a required member %q\", \"kind\")\n52|\t}\n53|\tkind, ok := rawString(kindValue)\n54|\tif !ok {\n55|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis kind is not a string\")\n56|\t}\n57|\tswitch kind {\n58|\tcase \"ax_session\":\n59|\t\treturn decodeAXSessionBasis(members)\n60|\tcase \"external_native\":\n61|\t\treturn decodeExternalNativeBasis(members)\n62|\tdefault:\n63|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis kind is outside ax_session|external_native\")\n64|\t}\n65|}\n66|\n67|func decodeAXSessionBasis(members map[string]json.RawMessage) (SourceBasis, error) {\n68|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, sourceBasisAXMembers); unknown {\n69|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis carries unknown member %q\", name)\n70|\t}\n71|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, sourceBasisAXRequired); missing {\n72|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis misses a required member %q\", name)\n73|\t}\n74|\tsessionID, ok := checkUUIDv7(members[\"source_session_id\"])\n75|\tif !ok {\n76|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis source_session_id is not a UUIDv7\")\n77|\t}\n78|\trecordID, ok := checkDigest(members[\"source_session_record_id\"])\n79|\tif !ok {\n80|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis source_session_record_id is not a digest\")\n81|\t}\n82|\tcheckpointID, ok := checkDigest(members[\"source_checkpoint_id\"])\n83|\tif !ok {\n84|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis source_checkpoint_id is not a digest\")\n85|\t}\n86|\tproviderID, ok := checkDigest(members[\"source_provider_identity_record_id\"])\n87|\tif !ok {\n88|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis source_provider_identity_record_id is not a digest\")\n89|\t}\n90|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n91|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n92|\t}\n93|\treturn SourceBasis{\n94|\t\tKind:                     \"ax_session\",\n95|\t\tSourceSessionID:          &sessionID,\n96|\t\tSourceSessionRecordID:    &recordID,\n97|\t\tSourceCheckpointID:       &checkpointID,\n98|\t\tSourceProviderIdentityID: &providerID,\n99|\t}, nil\n100|}\n101|\n102|func decodeExternalNativeBasis(members map[string]json.RawMessage) (SourceBasis, error) {\n103|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, sourceBasisExternalMembers); unknown {\n104|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis carries unknown member %q\", name)\n105|\t}\n106|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, sourceBasisExternalRequired); missing {\n107|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis misses a required member %q\", name)\n108|\t}\n109|\treference, ok := checkStringBounds(members[\"external_source_ref\"], 1, 512)\n110|\tif !ok {\n111|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis external_source_ref is not a string[1..512]\")\n112|\t}\n113|\tif err := SanitizeNativeKey(reference); err != nil {\n114|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, err\n115|\t}\n116|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n117|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, invalid(\"source basis extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n118|\t}\n119|\treturn SourceBasis{Kind: \"external_native\", ExternalSourceRef: &reference}, nil\n120|}\n121|\n122|// SourceBasisInput is one caller-supplied source basis candidate for\n123|// Build. Exactly the kind-selected fields must be set.\n124|type SourceBasisInput struct {\n125|\tKind                     string\n126|\tSourceSessionID          string\n127|\tSourceSessionRecordID    string\n128|\tSourceCheckpointID       string\n129|\tSourceProviderIdentityID string\n130|\tExternalSourceRef        string\n131|}\n132|\n133|func buildSourceBasis(input SourceBasisInput) (SourceBasis, map[string]any, error) {\n134|\tswitch input.Kind {\n135|\tcase \"ax_session\":\n136|\t\tsessionID, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(input.SourceSessionID)\n137|\t\tif err != nil {\n138|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis source_session_id is not a UUIDv7: %v\", err)\n139|\t\t}\n140|\t\trecordID, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.SourceSessionRecordID)\n141|\t\tif err != nil {\n142|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis source_session_record_id is not a digest: %v\", err)\n143|\t\t}\n144|\t\tcheckpointID, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.SourceCheckpointID)\n145|\t\tif err != nil {\n146|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis source_checkpoint_id is not a digest: %v\", err)\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t\tproviderID, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.SourceProviderIdentityID)\n149|\t\tif err != nil {\n150|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis source_provider_identity_record_id is not a digest: %v\", err)\n151|\t\t}\n152|\t\tif input.ExternalSourceRef != \"\" {\n153|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis ax_session carries an external source reference\")\n154|\t\t}\n155|\t\tbasis := SourceBasis{\n156|\t\t\tKind:                     \"ax_session\",\n157|\t\t\tSourceSessionID:          &sessionID,\n158|\t\t\tSourceSessionRecordID:    &recordID,\n159|\t\t\tSourceCheckpointID:       &checkpointID,\n160|\t\t\tSourceProviderIdentityID: &providerID,\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t\treturn basis, map[string]any{\n163|\t\t\t\"kind\":                               \"ax_session\",\n164|\t\t\t\"source_session_id\":                  sessionID.String(),\n165|\t\t\t\"source_session_record_id\":           recordID.String(),\n166|\t\t\t\"source_checkpoint_id\":               checkpointID.String(),\n167|\t\t\t\"source_provider_identity_record_id\": providerID.String(),\n168|\t\t\t\"extensions\":                         map[string]any{},\n169|\t\t}, nil\n170|\tcase \"external_native\":\n171|\t\tif stringLength(input.ExternalSourceRef) < 1 || stringLength(input.ExternalSourceRef) > 512 {\n172|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis external_source_ref is not a string[1..512]\")\n173|\t\t}\n174|\t\tif err := SanitizeNativeKey(input.ExternalSourceRef); err != nil {\n175|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, err\n176|\t\t}\n177|\t\tif input.SourceSessionID != \"\" || input.SourceSessionRecordID != \"\" ||\n178|\t\t\tinput.SourceCheckpointID != \"\" || input.SourceProviderIdentityID != \"\" {\n179|\t\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis external_native carries ax_session members\")\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\tbasis := SourceBasis{Kind: \"external_native\", ExternalSourceRef: &input.ExternalSourceRef}\n182|\t\treturn basis, map[string]any{\n183|\t\t\t\"kind\":                \"external_native\",\n184|\t\t\t\"external_source_ref\": input.ExternalSourceRef,\n185|\t\t\t\"extensions\":          map[string]any{},\n186|\t\t}, nil\n187|\tdefault:\n188|\t\treturn SourceBasis{}, nil, invalid(\"source basis kind is outside ax_session|external_native\")\n189|\t}\n190|}\n191|\n192|// StableSnapshotProof is one validated stable snapshot proof.\n193|type StableSnapshotProof struct {\n194|\tProofKind         string\n195|\tSourceGeneration  Generation\n196|\tSnapshotIdentity  *scalar.Digest\n197|\tPreCaptureDigest  scalar.Digest\n198|\tPostCaptureDigest scalar.Digest\n199|\tInputBlocked      bool\n200|\tForegroundIdle    bool\n201|\tBackgroundIdle    bool\n202|}\n203|\n204|var proofKinds = []string{\n205|\t\"closed_store\",\n206|\t\"immutable_snapshot\",\n207|\t\"verified_log_prefix\",\n208|\t\"provider_quiescence\",\n209|}\n210|\n211|func validProofKind(kind string) bool {\n212|\tfor _, allowed := range proofKinds {\n213|\t\tif kind == allowed {\n214|\t\t\treturn true\n215|\t\t}\n216|\t}\n217|\treturn false\n218|}\n219|\n220|var stableProofMembers = map[string]bool{\n221|\t\"proof_kind\": true, \"source_generation\": true, \"snapshot_identity_digest\": true,\n222|\t\"pre_capture_digest\": true, \"post_capture_digest\": true,\n223|\t\"input_blocked\": true, \"foreground_idle\": true, \"background_idle\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n224|}\n225|\n226|var stableProofRequired = []string{\n227|\t\"proof_kind\", \"source_generation\", \"snapshot_identity_digest\",\n228|\t\"pre_capture_digest\", \"post_capture_digest\",\n229|\t\"input_blocked\", \"foreground_idle\", \"background_idle\", \"extensions\",\n230|}\n231|\n232|// DecodeStableSnapshotProof validates one closed StableSnapshotProof:\n233|// equal capture digests, the proof-kind/identity/boolean coupling,\n234|// and the immutable generation token.\n235|func DecodeStableSnapshotProof(raw json.RawMessage) (StableSnapshotProof, error) {\n236|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n237|\tif fault != nil {\n238|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof %s (%s)\", fault.detail, memberField(fault.member))\n239|\t}\n240|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, stableProofMembers); unknown {\n241|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof carries unknown member %q\", name)\n242|\t}\n243|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, stableProofRequired); missing {\n244|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof misses a required member %q\", name)\n245|\t}\n246|\tkind, ok := rawString(members[\"proof_kind\"])\n247|\tif !ok || !validProofKind(kind) {\n248|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof kind is outside the closed proof vocabulary\")\n249|\t}\n250|\tgeneration, ok := checkGeneration(members[\"source_generation\"])\n251|\tif !ok {\n252|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof source_generation is not a string[1..512]\")\n253|\t}\n254|\tvar identity *scalar.Digest\n255|\tif !isNull(members[\"snapshot_identity_digest\"]) {\n256|\t\tvalue, ok := checkDigest(members[\"snapshot_identity_digest\"])\n257|\t\tif !ok {\n258|\t\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof snapshot_identity_digest is not a digest\")\n259|\t\t}\n260|\t\tidentity = &value\n261|\t}\n262|\tpre, ok := checkDigest(members[\"pre_capture_digest\"])\n263|\tif !ok {\n264|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof pre_capture_digest is not a digest\")\n265|\t}\n266|\tpost, ok := checkDigest(members[\"post_capture_digest\"])\n267|\tif !ok {\n268|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof post_capture_digest is not a digest\")\n269|\t}\n270|\tinputBlocked, ok := rawBool(members[\"input_blocked\"])\n271|\tif !ok {\n272|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof input_blocked is not a boolean\")\n273|\t}\n274|\tforegroundIdle, ok := rawBool(members[\"foreground_idle\"])\n275|\tif !ok {\n276|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof foreground_idle is not a boolean\")\n277|\t}\n278|\tbackgroundIdle, ok := rawBool(members[\"background_idle\"])\n279|\tif !ok {\n280|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof background_idle is not a boolean\")\n281|\t}\n282|\tproof := StableSnapshotProof{\n283|\t\tProofKind:         kind,\n284|\t\tSourceGeneration:  generation,\n285|\t\tSnapshotIdentity:  identity,\n286|\t\tPreCaptureDigest:  pre,\n287|\t\tPostCaptureDigest: post,\n288|\t\tInputBlocked:      inputBlocked,\n289|\t\tForegroundIdle:    foregroundIdle,\n290|\t\tBackgroundIdle:    backgroundIdle,\n291|\t}\n292|\tif err := checkProofCoupling(proof); err != nil {\n293|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, err\n294|\t}\n295|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n296|\t\treturn StableSnapshotProof{}, invalid(\"stable snapshot proof extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n297|\t}\n298|\treturn proof, nil\n299|}\n300|\n301|// checkProofCoupling enforces the proof-kind/identity/boolean\n302|// coupling: capture digests are equal (size equality is never\n303|// proof and is not consulted); closed-store and\n304|// provider-quiescence require all booleans true and null snapshot\n305|// identity; immutable-snapshot and log-prefix require non-null\n306|// identity.\n307|func checkProofCoupling(proof StableSnapshotProof) error {\n308|\tif err := CheckDigestsEqual(proof.PreCaptureDigest, proof.PostCaptureDigest); err != nil {\n309|\t\treturn invalid(\"stable snapshot proof: %v\", err)\n310|\t}\n311|\tswitch proof.ProofKind {\n312|\tcase \"closed_store\", \"provider_quiescence\":\n313|\t\tif proof.SnapshotIdentity != nil {\n314|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"stable snapshot proof %s requires null snapshot identity\", proof.ProofKind)\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t\tif !proof.InputBlocked || !proof.ForegroundIdle || !proof.BackgroundIdle {\n317|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"stable snapshot proof %s requires input_blocked, foreground_idle, and background_idle\", proof.ProofKind)\n318|\t\t}\n319|\tcase \"immutable_snapshot\", \"verified_log_prefix\":\n320|\t\tif proof.SnapshotIdentity == nil {\n321|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"stable snapshot proof %s requires non-null snapshot identity\", proof.ProofKind)\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t}\n324|\treturn nil\n325|}\n326|\n327|// CaptureBoundary is one validated Capture Boundary.\n328|type CaptureBoundary struct {\n329|\tKind              string\n330|\tProof             *StableSnapshotProof\n331|\tSourceGeneration  *Generation\n332|\tPreCaptureDigest  *scalar.Digest\n333|\tPostCaptureDigest *scalar.Digest\n334|}\n335|\n336|// Stable reports whether the boundary is the stable form.\n337|func (boundary CaptureBoundary) Stable() bool { return boundary.Kind == \"stable\" }\n338|\n339|var stableBoundaryMembers = map[string]bool{\n340|\t\"kind\": true, \"proof\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n341|}\n342|\n343|var stableBoundaryRequired = []string{\"kind\", \"proof\", \"extensions\"}\n344|\n345|var unstableBoundaryMembers = map[string]bool{\n346|\t\"kind\": true, \"source_generation\": true, \"pre_capture_digest\": true,\n347|\t\"post_capture_digest\": true, \"reason_code\": true,\n348|\t\"operator_explicit\": true, \"target_projection_forbidden\": true, \"extensions\": true,\n349|}\n350|\n351|var unstableBoundaryRequired = []string{\n352|\t\"kind\", \"source_generation\", \"pre_capture_digest\",\n353|\t\"post_capture_digest\", \"reason_code\",\n354|\t\"operator_explicit\", \"target_projection_forbidden\", \"extensions\",\n355|}\n356|\n357|// DecodeCaptureBoundary validates one closed Capture Boundary.\n358|func DecodeCaptureBoundary(raw json.RawMessage) (CaptureBoundary, error) {\n359|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(bytesTrimSpace(raw))\n360|\tif fault != nil {\n361|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary %s (%s)\", fault.detail, memberField(fault.member))\n362|\t}\n363|\tkindValue, present := members[\"kind\"]\n364|\tif !present {\n365|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary misses a required member %q\", \"kind\")\n366|\t}\n367|\tkind, ok := rawString(kindValue)\n368|\tif !ok {\n369|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary kind is not a string\")\n370|\t}\n371|\tswitch kind {\n372|\tcase \"stable\":\n373|\t\treturn decodeStableBoundary(members)\n374|\tcase \"unstable_archive\":\n375|\t\treturn decodeUnstableBoundary(members)\n376|\tdefault:\n377|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary kind is outside stable|unstable_archive\")\n378|\t}\n379|}\n380|\n381|func decodeStableBoundary(members map[string]json.RawMessage) (CaptureBoundary, error) {\n382|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, stableBoundaryMembers); unknown {\n383|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary carries unknown member %q\", name)\n384|\t}\n385|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, stableBoundaryRequired); missing {\n386|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary misses a required member %q\", name)\n387|\t}\n388|\tproof, err := DecodeStableSnapshotProof(members[\"proof\"])\n389|\tif err != nil {\n390|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, err\n391|\t}\n392|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n393|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n394|\t}\n395|\treturn CaptureBoundary{Kind: \"stable\", Proof: &proof}, nil\n396|}\n397|\n398|func decodeUnstableBoundary(members map[string]json.RawMessage) (CaptureBoundary, error) {\n399|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, unstableBoundaryMembers); unknown {\n400|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary carries unknown member %q\", name)\n401|\t}\n402|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, unstableBoundaryRequired); missing {\n403|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary misses a required member %q\", name)\n404|\t}\n405|\tgeneration, ok := checkGeneration(members[\"source_generation\"])\n406|\tif !ok {\n407|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary source_generation is not a string[1..512]\")\n408|\t}\n409|\tpre, ok := checkDigest(members[\"pre_capture_digest\"])\n410|\tif !ok {\n411|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary pre_capture_digest is not a digest\")\n412|\t}\n413|\tpost, ok := checkDigest(members[\"post_capture_digest\"])\n414|\tif !ok {\n415|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary post_capture_digest is not a digest\")\n416|\t}\n417|\treason, ok := rawString(members[\"reason_code\"])\n418|\tif !ok || reason != \"source_not_quiescent\" {\n419|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary reason_code is not source_not_quiescent\")\n420|\t}\n421|\texplicit, ok := rawBool(members[\"operator_explicit\"])\n422|\tif !ok || !explicit {\n423|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary operator_explicit is not true\")\n424|\t}\n425|\tforbidden, ok := rawBool(members[\"target_projection_forbidden\"])\n426|\tif !ok || !forbidden {\n427|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary target_projection_forbidden is not true\")\n428|\t}\n429|\tif extensionsFault := checkExtensionsClosed(members[\"extensions\"]); extensionsFault != nil {\n430|\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, invalid(\"capture boundary extensions %s\", extensionsFault)\n431|\t}\n432|\treturn CaptureBoundary{\n433|\t\tKind:              \"unstable_archive\",\n434|\t\tSourceGeneration:  &generation,\n435|\t\tPreCaptureDigest:  &pre,\n436|\t\tPostCaptureDigest: &post,\n437|\t}, nil\n438|}\n439|\n440|// RefuseUnstableForTarget is the G2 target-branch gate: the unstable\n441|// archive form is core-created archive-only output and can never\n442|// enter a target branch, so target admission refuses it.\n443|func RefuseUnstableForTarget(boundary CaptureBoundary) error {\n444|\tif boundary.Kind == \"unstable_archive\" {\n445|\t\treturn invalid(\"capture boundary unstable_archive cannot enter a target branch\")\n446|\t}\n447|\tif boundary.Kind != \"stable\" {\n448|\t\treturn invalid(\"capture boundary kind is outside stable|unstable_archive\")\n449|\t}\n450|\treturn nil\n451|}\n452|\n453|// BoundaryInput is one caller-supplied capture boundary candidate\n454|// for Build. Core must be true to construct the unstable archive\n455|// form; only core may construct it. Core is a caller assertion at\n456|// this entry, so \"only core may construct\" is nominal here: the\n457|// real protection is RefuseUnstableForTarget, which refuses every\n458|// unstable archive at target-branch admission regardless of who\n459|// constructed it.\n460|type BoundaryInput struct {\n461|\tKind              string\n462|\tProofKind         string\n463|\tGeneration        string\n464|\tSnapshotIdentity  *string\n465|\tPreCaptureDigest  string\n466|\tPostCaptureDigest string\n467|\tInputBlocked      bool\n468|\tForegroundIdle    bool\n469|\tBackgroundIdle    bool\n470|\tCore              bool\n471|}\n472|\n473|func buildBoundary(input BoundaryInput) (CaptureBoundary, map[string]any, error) {\n474|\tswitch input.Kind {\n475|\tcase \"stable\":\n476|\t\tproof, object, err := buildStableProof(input)\n477|\t\tif err != nil {\n478|\t\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, nil, err\n479|\t\t}\n480|\t\tboundary := CaptureBoundary{Kind: \"stable\", Proof: &proof}\n481|\t\treturn boundary, map[string]any{\n482|\t\t\t\"kind\":       \"stable\",\n483|\t\t\t\"proof\":      object,\n484|\t\t\t\"extensions\": map[string]any{},\n485|\t\t}, nil\n486|\tcase \"unstable_archive\":\n487|\t\tif !input.Core {\n488|\t\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, nil, invalid(\"capture boundary unstable_archive is core-created only\")\n489|\t\t}\n490|\t\tgeneration, err := ParseGeneration(input.Generation)\n491|\t\tif err != nil {\n492|\t\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, nil, err\n493|\t\t}\n494|\t\tpre, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.PreCaptureDigest)\n495|\t\tif err != nil {\n496|\t\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, nil, invalid(\"capture boundary pre_capture_digest is not a digest: %v\", err)\n497|\t\t}\n498|\t\tpost, err := scalar.ParseDigest(input.PostCaptureDigest)\n499|\t\tif err != nil {\n500|\t\t\treturn CaptureBoundary{}, nil, invalid(\"capture boundary post_capture_digest is not a digest: %v\", err)\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
