identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\nblob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\nthe package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\nmaps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\nsibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\nresult, and no runtime capability claim.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\ngo test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n```\\n\\n## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n\\n[`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\ncrash/restart outcome gate over the landed checkpoint and journal owners. Its\\nboundary registry enumerates all 94 crash boundaries of the pinned Section\\n13.13 table plus the `CR-CLONE` prose range, verified against the pinned text\\nby a derivation test rather than a hand-typed list; each boundary is\\n=== secprim guard/path API ===\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:29:func CheckMemberPath(platform scalar.Platform, member string) error {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:58:func unwrapPercentEncoding(value string) string {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:75:func containsEncodedDot(member string) bool {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:82:func containsOverlongSeparator(member string) bool {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:89:func memberErrorTarget(member string) string {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:102:type Guard struct {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:113:func NewGuard(root string, platform scalar.Platform, managed []string) (Guard, error) {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:141:func (guard Guard) Resolve(member string) (string, error) {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:161:func (guard Guard) slashRoot() string {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:171:func joinSlash(slashRoot, member string) string {\\ninternal/secprim/path.go:184:func withinRoot(slashRo