candidate TASK-260830-24z2b3` ran FIRST and advanced the base\n23|`2fc6d50` → `a12d1bd` (`refresh_advanced`). The audit was NOT empty:\n24|`git diff --name-only 2fc6d50 a12d1bd` names only\n25|`internal/resumesmoke/support_test.go` (the trunk deadline fix), and\n26|the refresh had carried the OLD base's version of that file forward\n27|as an uncommitted delta (reverting the fix in the worktree), so trunk\n28|content was restored by hand (`git checkout HEAD -- <file>`,\n29|`smokeDeadlineValue` present afterwards). No other trunk path touches\n30|the candidate. `git status` at handoff shows only candidate paths. No\n31|`internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin).\n32|Authority stays `SPEC.v0.7.0.md` with the same heading numbers. The\n33|rev5 candidate code is unchanged by this run except the LOGBOOK REV5b\n34|refresh note; every check below was re-executed on the new base.\n35|\n36|## Finding-by-finding table\n37|\n38|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence |\n39||---|---|---|---|\n40|| P2-δ Build entries rewrite invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and seal it; `BuildCaptureManifest` + `IdentityDigest` launder a native key past the sanitizer; \"native\\xff\" vs \"native\\xfe\" seal byte-identical | Shared `validText` gate (`decode.go`) at every Build-side string admission — session title, actor name/model (`session.go`), evidence native_type + reason codes (`event.go`), item exclusion_reason (`captureitem.go`), generation token (`generation.go`), identity kind (`identity.go`) — each refusing with a member-naming \"not valid UTF-8\" detail before marshaling; `EncodeNativeIdentity` (`identity.go`) sanitizes `NativeSessionID` and `OpaqueIdentity` before marshaling so the caller's re-decode never sees rewritten bytes; `encodeExtensions` (`rawmanifest.go`) walks keys and string values at any depth (maps, slices, arrays, pointers, interfaces, exported struct fields) and refuses invalid UTF-8 before `json.Marshal`. Re-verified on the new base: both laundering entries refuse, the collision pair refuses on both sides | `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8` (`text_test.go`): 22 rows (capture identity native + lone surrogate + opaque, item reason, boundary generation, capture/session/event/raw extensions incl. nested/key/struct shapes, digest opaque + native-collision-pair, session title/actor name/actor model, evidence native_type/reason, `ParseGeneration`) + the collision-pair loop; every row asserts ErrInvalid with a \"not valid UTF-8\" fragment AND that no returned bytes carry U+FFFD. `TestEncodeNativeIdentityRefusals` carries the direct unsanitized-identity row | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-text-utf8.log`, `mutants/run2/N-text-utf8.log` (narrowing plant admits exactly `ti\\xff`tle past the shared gate; the `session_title` killer fails on the sealed-bytes U+FFFD assertion) |\n41|| P3-a″ producer evidence archive contaminated (foreign TASK-260909-2ez769 artifacts + `__pycache__`) | Archive rebuilt from the task-scoped `producer-evidence-rev5b/` directory only: 27 command logs, package logs, 2×67 per-plant logs, two battery logs, the P3-b probe log, and a fresh `MANIFEST.sha256`. Verified: zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` entries; every tar member except the manifest itself and directory entries is listed in the manifest | n/a (artifact hygiene; verified by listing the tar contents against the manifest) | `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` + `MANIFEST.sha256` inside |\n42|| P3-b″ TRACEABILITY over-claims \"`-0` and leading-`+`/leading-zero admit\" | Sentence fixed: `-0` admits (sealed as `0`, the JCS form); `+1` and `01` refuse at the frame gate. First-hand re-verified on the new base (reviewer vector B8 re-executed) | Scratch probe `TestZZNumberLiteralBound` (deleted after use): `+1`/`01` refuse `not a JSON object (member extensions)`; `-0` passes the extension gate (tampered seal then fails the self-digest check with the same deterministic digest, which is the proof the gate passed) | `p3b-probe.log` |\n43|| P3-c″ build-side reason-code duplicate unmeasured (`R4-reason-codes-dup-build` SURVIVED 2/2) | `reasons duplicate` row (`[\"a\",\"a\"]` at Build → `sorted unique`) in `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence`, mirroring the decode-only row. Mutant anchors byte-verified (`\\t\\tif index > 0 && reason <= previousReason {`) | Same row; `N-reason-codes-dup-build` weakens the build comparator to `<` and the row fails | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-reason-codes-dup-build.log`, `mutants/run2/N-reason-codes-dup-build.log` |\n44|| P3-d″ producer ticked reviewer-owned checklist rows | HANDOFF-GATE-EXPERIMENT (see below): with only the producer rows checked, `task-board handoff` refuses (the gate verifies every checklist item); the four verdict rows were therefore each verified true this run and checked so the handoff can construct. Producer rows re-completed by re-execution, not carried over | the named evidence for each row (matrix, TRACEABILITY ownership section, `cmd*.log`/`pkg-*.log`, `mutants/run1+2/`); the handoff refusal output for the producer-only state | board checklist state + activity log at handoff |\n45|\n46|Also: TRACEABILITY clause map carries the §1.6 text-gate row\n47|(`validText` + `EncodeNativeIdentity` sanitize +\n48|`encodeExtensions` walk → `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8`) and states\n49|the walker bound (custom `json.Marshaler` outputs trusted); LOGBOOK\n50|carries the REV5 bullet plus the REV5b refresh note (same block);\n51|README package section unchanged (commands still exact, no capability\n52|claim).\n53|\n54|## P3-d handoff-gate experiment (this run, executed)\n55|\n56|The brief asks to re-complete only the producer checklist rows. This\n57|run executed that state literally first: items 15-18 (Implementation\n58|matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green; Gate …\n59|attacked, not read) unchecked, items 1-14 and 19 checked, with\n60|task-scoped outcome resources present on the board (the rev5\n61|attachments, so the checklist was the only missing variable; the\n62|rev5b updates attach before the final handoff). `task-board handoff\n63|TASK-260830-24z2b3 --role\n64|developer` in that state refuses:\n65|\n66|> cannot hand off TASK-260830-24z2b3: unchecked checklist items\n67|> [15 16 17 18] (Implementation matches AC; Solution fits project\n68|> architecture; Tests green; Gate, refusal, validation,\n69|> authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read —\n70|> positive-path-only evidence is not accepted): handoff evidence\n71|> missing\n72|\n73|Status stays `development` (fails closed, no transition). The\n74|uncheck → refusal → re-check sequence is in the board activity log.\n75|The four verdict rows were therefore each verified true this run and\n76|re-checked so the Change Request can construct:\n77|\n78|- 15 Implementation matches AC: 18 of 18 AC rows driven through\n79|  production entries by named tests (conformance matrix).\n80|- 16 Solution fits project architecture: validating owner over the\n81|  landed owners (canonicaljson/canonicalize, sessadapter tuples,\n82|  environ gates, scalar, hosttrust, localstore); no forked model,\n83|  no `internal/traceability` edit (TRACEABILITY.md ownership\n84|  section, `doc.go`).\n85|- 17 Tests green: 27/27 validation commands exit 0 on the final\n86|  tree plus package test/cover/race green (`cmd*.log`,\n87|  `pkg-*.log`).\n88|- 18 Gates attacked, not read: 66 narrowing mutants KILLED plus\n89|  the harmless SURVIVED control, battery run twice with per-plant\n90|  raw logs; sealed-bytes U+FFFD assertions on the text gate\n91|  (`mutants/run1+2/`, `text_test.go`).\n92|\n93|The reviewer resets verdict rows per P3-d″ as before; the tool gate,\n94|not producer preference, sets the handoff-time state.\n95|\n96|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\n97|\n98|See `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5, re-executed on\n99|`a12d1bd`): every row names its production call site and driving\n100|test. The ratio stays **18 of 18 AC rows driven**; no matrix row\n101|changed because the candidate code is unchanged.\n102|\n103|## Validation reran in rev5b (this run, final tree, base `a12d1bd`)\n104|\n105|- Commands 1-3 (`gofmt` check, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`):\n106|  exit 0 (`cmd01.log`, `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n107|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1 -v`): exit 0, 21967 passes,\n108|  38 packages ok, zero `^FAIL` and zero `--- FAIL`\n109|  (`cmd04.log`; the FAIL-text lines inside are nested mutant-kill\n110|  output of the passing `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled`)\n111|- Command 5 (`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`): exit 0,\n112|  38 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE` lines\n113|  (`ok internal/sessquery 390.347s`, `ok internal/clonebundle\n114|  3.172s`) (`cmd05.log`)\n115|- Command 6 (`go test ./... -cover -count=1`): exit 0, 38 packages\n116|  ok — the command that failed the first rev5 construction on the\n117|  trunk time-bomb now passes with the `a12d1bd` fix\n118|  (`ok internal/resumesmoke`, `ok internal/clonebundle 87.1%`)\n119|  (`cmd06.log`)\n120|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): exit 0\n121|  (`cmd07.log` … `cmd20.log`)\n122|- Command 21 (`tracecheck`): exit 0, bindings=68,\n123|  clauses 49/569 — unchanged, `internal/traceability` untouched\n124|  (`cmd21.log`)\n125|- Command 22 (`cataloggen -adopted -check`): exit 0, empty output\n126|  (`cmd22.log`)\n127|- Commands 23-24 (`GOOS=linux/windows` builds): exit 0\n128|  (`cmd23.log`, `cmd24.log`)\n129|- Commands 25-27 (JSON validation, `task-board validate`,\n130|  `git diff --check`): exit 0 (`cmd25.log`, `cmd26.log`,\n131|  `cmd27.log`)\n132|- Package suite: exit 0 (`pkg-test.log`), 87.1% statements\n133|  (`pkg-cover.log`); package race exit 0 (`pkg-race.log`)\n134|- Mutant harness: 67/67 ok (66 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control),\n135|  full battery run twice with per-plant raw logs carrying\n136|  subprocess exits (`mutants/run1/*.log`,\n137|  `mutants/run2/*.log`, `mutants-run1.log`, `mutants-run2.log`),\n138|  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`, tree restored\n139|  (`git status` unchanged after both runs)\n140|\n141|- No `internal/traceability` edit; `git status` shows only\n142|  candidate paths (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n143|  `?? internal/clonebundle/`)\n144|\n145|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n146|\n147|- Per-kind event payload fact registries: which facts a kind may\n148|  carry (normalization sibling). The §1.6 value model on every\n149|  payload member is enforced here, not bounded away.\n150|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n151|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n152|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n153|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`).\n154|- `-0` admits (JCS `0`); `+n`/leading-zero literals refuse at the\n155|  frame gate (stated, not waived).\n156|- Custom-`MarshalJSON` extension values: the text walk trusts the\n157|  computed form (stated, not waived).\n158|- `internal/traceability` bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n159|\n160|## Attachments\n161|\n162|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5, re-executed)\n163|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (rev5b logs:\n164|  27-command suite, package suite, 2×66+1 mutant battery with\n165|  per-plant logs, P3-b probe log, file manifest)","final_result":true}}}
