{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dbf5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b225-c4f5-7551-94b6-c0c601dc074b"},"sequence":3157,"recorded_at":1780531400006309,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"83118e98-b6d0-4b7d-9792-f7c513af3eac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b240-0fc6-7022-9562-979e78a992d1"},"task_id":"01a0b240-0fc6-7022-9562-979e78a992d1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b240-0fc6-7022-9562-979e78a992d1","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-17\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\n+\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\n+- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the gate-verified pre digest for both capture digests — production bytes are identical to sealing the measurement, and the `N-race-order-capture` / `N-race-order-project` mutants prove the gate precedes the seal and the receipt (sealing the raw post measurement would fail closed under a reorder and leave the ordering unpinned). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 28 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n","final_result":true}}}
